WEB SOURCE (the specification — read end to end)
  web/src/components/feedback/AlertBanner.tsx — a presentational, page-level inline notification:
    AlertBanner({ variant, title?, children, onClose?, icon? }) renders a tinted, backdrop-blurred,
    bordered box (flex items-start gap-3 rounded-xl border p-4) with:
      • an optional leading icon (shrink-0, titleText tint),
      • an optional emphasised title line (text-sm font-medium, titleText tint),
      • the required message line (children; text-xs, text tint; mt-0.5 only when a title is present),
      • an optional trailing dismiss (X) button (onClose; hover bg-white/[0.06]).
    `alertVariantMap` keys border-X/20 · bg-X/5 · text-X/80 · titleText text-X off the variant union
    'info' | 'success' | 'warning' | 'danger'. The component is "anonymous": it has NO t() calls — the
    caller supplies the strings (prompt "Titles / labels / i18n keys: none extracted — surface is anonymous").
  Documented data sources / consumers (the AlertBanner doc comment is explicit):
    • useMutationToast (web/src/api/hooks/_toastHelpers.ts) — every user mutation emits success(title) or
      error(err, title); the error path shows the title plus the underlying err.message as a secondary line.
    • LiveStaleDataBanner (web/src/components/feedback/LiveStaleDataBanner.tsx) — wraps
      <AlertBanner variant="warning" icon=WifiOff> when the live pipe has been disconnected ≥ 2 minutes.
    • OfflineBanner (web/src/components/feedback/OfflineBanner.tsx) — wraps <AlertBanner variant="warning"
      icon=WifiOff> while the browser is offline (cached data shown).
  These three consumers are THE data the prompt's "Data sources: useMutationToast" + the required
  loading/empty/error/stale/offline states map onto.

SCOPE / ARCHITECTURE NOTE  (no silent drift — disclosed in full)
  The ATOMIC banner primitive already exists: Sources/Components/Feedback/Banners.swift `TSAlertBanner`
  ("Base banner (web AlertBanner)") + its named presets (TSOfflineBanner, TSLiveStaleDataBanner, …). That
  atomic component is OUT OF SCOPE here (prompt "Out of Scope: Atomic shared components (covered by the P4
  component-library bundle prompt)"). This 0113 SHARED SURFACE is therefore the higher-level, DATA-BOUND,
  multi-state AlertBanner HOST — the surface that binds the mutation-toast bus + the live-connection holder
  (P1/S8), renders every state, and emits the P1/S11 view.opened telemetry. It reproduces the web AlertBanner
  composition as scoped subviews (tinted title + message via the SI status tokens; facade-resolved strings via
  Text(verbatim:)) rather than calling TSAlertBanner, for two parity reasons: (a) the web tints BOTH title and
  message (TSAlertBanner uses neutral text), and (b) the P1/S10 facade resolves to String, incompatible with
  TSAlertBanner's LocalizedStringKey API. This mirrors the established precedent where AiUsageCard (0237) /
  AIUsageCard (0203) reproduce the shared <UsageCard> regions as scoped subviews for the same facade reason.

